From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: mask the autoneg interrupt while the
 AQR113C wake is armed

Arming wake on the AQR113C (aqr113c_wol_settings(true)) ends with
genphy_c45_restart_aneg(), which drops the link and renegotiates it a few
seconds later. aqr_config_intr() leaves the vendor autoneg interrupt unmasked
(VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK_AN), so the link-up event drives INT_N, which the
Jetson wires to the SoC as a PMC wake (the "mgbe" event). The status is cleared
only by aqr_handle_interrupt(), which does not run in a suspended system. The
board therefore resumes a few seconds after it suspends, before any packet.

Measured on a Jetson AGX Orin with the 10G port connected: with wake armed the
system woke 8 s and 13 s after suspend entry in two runs, against a 300 s timer.

NVIDIA's R39 6.8 kernel masks that interrupt when arming and unmasks it again
when disarming, in the same function. The 6.18 port of the change lost both
lines. Restore them.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fixes up NVIDIA's out-of-tree Tegra series]
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
@@ -1447,6 +1447,10 @@
 			return ret;
 		val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK);
 		val |= VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK_GBE;
+		/* Mask the autoneg interrupt while armed: the restart below drops
+		 * and renegotiates the link, and that event must not wake the system.
+		 */
+		val &= ~VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK_AN;
 		ret = phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK, val);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
@@ -1472,6 +1476,13 @@
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
+		/* Unmask the autoneg interrupt again */
+		val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK);
+		val |= VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK_AN;
+		ret = phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_INT_VEND_MASK, val);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+
 		/* Restore the SERDES/System Interface back to the XFI mode */
 		ret = phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1,
 				    VEND1_GLOBAL_CFG_100M, VEND1_GLOBAL_SYS_CONFIG_XFI);
